---
/**
 * Privacy policy.
 *
 * **This page states what the system actually does. It has not been through
 * legal review, and it must be before launch** — see docs/brief.md, "Claims
 * held for confirmation", and the plan's open items. Everything below is
 * sourced from the code and the decisions record rather than from the old
 * policy, and each claim is checkable:
 *
 *   fields collected      forms/schema.sql, docs/decisions.md "Enquiry form fields"
 *   IP / user-agent       forms/schema.sql (remote_ip, user_agent, page_path)
 *   the classifier        henley-utils modules/spam_classifier.py — an LLM call,
 *                         six categories, reading name/email/phone/message
 *   Salesforce            update_salesforce_leads.py, WebFormID_c__c upsert
 *   reception digest      non_sales_enquiry_notifications.py, over Microsoft 365
 *   analytics             GTM-PGSH3HF7, gtag GT-TXH3QGV, two Google Ads click
 *                         conversions on tel: and mailto:
 *   maintenance form      a Microsoft Form, site.ts MAINTENANCE_FORM
 *
 * The old policy was four paragraphs that said a contact form existed and that
 * information is not sold. It did not mention Salesforce, Microsoft, Google or
 * an AI classification step, and it did not say that anything leaves Australia
 * — which, under APP 8, is the disclosure that matters most here.
 *
 * Two things this page deliberately does not do. It does not claim the site is
 * secure — the old wording's "commercially acceptable means" is the one honest
 * sentence in it and is kept. And it does not treat "we replied to your
 * enquiry" and "we send you marketing" as one consent; the review asked for
 * those to stay distinct, so they are separate paragraphs with separate bases.
 */
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import PageHeader from '../components/PageHeader.astro';
import { EMAIL, PHONE, PHONE_HREF, ADDRESS } from '../site.ts';

const updated = '10 September 2026';
---

<Base
  title="Privacy policy | The Henley on Broadwater"
  description="How The Henley on Broadwater collects, uses, stores and discloses personal information from this website, and how to reach us about it."
>
  <PageHeader
    heading="Privacy policy"
    standfirst="What we collect through this website, what happens to it, and who else sees it."
  />

  <section class="band">
    <div class="wrap wrap--narrow prose">
      <p class="updated">Last updated {updated}</p>

      <p>
        This policy covers <strong>thehenley.com.au</strong> and is written to the
        Australian Privacy Principles in the Privacy Act 1988 (Cth). It describes the
        website. If you live here, or a member of your family does, your residence or
        care agreement and the documents given to you at the time govern the information
        held about you, and this policy does not replace them.
      </p>

      <h2>What we collect</h2>

      <h3>When you send an enquiry</h3>
      <p>The enquiry form asks for:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>your name and email address, which are required;</li>
        <li>your phone number and your message, which are optional;</li>
        <li>whether you are asking about apartment living, private aged care, or both.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>Submitting the form also records, without asking you:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>the page you sent it from;</li>
        <li>your IP address and the identifying string your browser sends;</li>
        <li>the date and time.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Those last three are kept for one reason: they let us tell a real enquiry from
        automated abuse, and they let us limit how often the form can be submitted from
        one place. They are not used to build a profile of you.
      </p>

      <h3>When you use the site</h3>
      <p>
        We use Google Analytics and Google Tag Manager to count visits and see which
        pages people read, and Google Ads records when someone clicks the phone number or
        the email address so we know which advertising is working. These set cookies in
        your browser and send Google your IP address and details of the pages you view.
        Our web server also keeps ordinary request logs.
      </p>
      <p>
        You can refuse or delete these cookies in your browser settings. Nothing on this
        site stops working if you do.
      </p>

      <h3>When you lodge a maintenance request</h3>
      <p>
        The residents' maintenance form is a Microsoft Form, not part of this website.
        What you enter there goes to Microsoft and then to our maintenance team.
      </p>

      <h2>What we do with an enquiry</h2>
      <p>When you send an enquiry, this happens:</p>
      <ol>
        <li>
          It is stored in a database on infrastructure The Henley controls, in Australia.
        </li>
        <li>
          An automated step reads your name, email address, phone number and message to
          sort genuine enquiries from spam and to work out who should answer — sales, or
          reception. <strong>That step uses an external artificial-intelligence
          service</strong>, so the content of your enquiry is sent to that provider to be
          classified. It is not used to train anybody's model, and no decision that
          affects you is made by it beyond which desk your enquiry lands on.
        </li>
        <li>
          If you are enquiring about living here, your details are added to Salesforce,
          the customer relationship system our sales team uses, so that someone can
          follow up and so we can see we have already spoken to you.
        </li>
        <li>
          Other enquiries are sent to reception in a summary email, using Microsoft 365.
        </li>
      </ol>
      <p>
        A person reads every enquiry that reaches either destination. Nothing is answered
        automatically.
      </p>

      <h2>Replying to you, and marketing</h2>
      <p>
        <strong>Replying is not marketing.</strong> If you ask us something, we will
        answer — by email or phone, using the details you gave us. That is the purpose you
        gave them to us for and it needs no further permission.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Marketing is separate and is your choice.</strong> We will only add you to
        a mailing list, or send you news and events you did not ask for, if you tell us
        you want that. If we ever do send you something like that, it will say who it is
        from and how to stop it, and stopping it takes one reply. You can also tell us at
        any time on the details below, and it will not affect anything else.
      </p>

      <h2>Who else sees it</h2>
      <p>
        We do not sell personal information, and we do not give it to anyone for their own
        marketing. It is handled by:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Salesforce</strong> — the sales team's customer relationship system.</li>
        <li><strong>Microsoft</strong> — email and Microsoft 365, and the maintenance form.</li>
        <li><strong>Google</strong> — analytics and advertising measurement.</li>
        <li>
          <strong>An artificial-intelligence provider</strong> — the classification step
          described above.
        </li>
        <li>
          Our IT and hosting providers, who can reach the systems in order to keep them
          running.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        <strong>Some of these store or process information outside Australia</strong>,
        including in the United States. That is the ordinary arrangement for services of
        this kind, and it means your information may be handled under another country's
        laws. We use these providers on their standard terms and do not permit them to use
        your information for their own purposes.
      </p>
      <p>
        We will also disclose information where the law requires it, or where it is
        necessary to prevent a serious threat to someone's life, health or safety.
      </p>

      <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
      <p>
        Enquiries are kept while there is a reason to — a live conversation, a record that
        we have already spoken, an obligation to keep records. If you ask us to delete
        yours and no such reason applies, we will.
      </p>

      <h2>Security</h2>
      <p>
        We take reasonable steps to protect the information we hold. But no transmission
        over the internet and no method of electronic storage is completely secure, and we
        cannot guarantee absolute security. Please do not send us sensitive information —
        health details, financial details, identity documents — through the enquiry form.
        Ring us instead.
      </p>

      <h2>Seeing, correcting or complaining about what we hold</h2>
      <p>
        You can ask us what personal information we hold about you, ask us to correct it,
        or complain about how we have handled it. Contact us and we will acknowledge it
        and respond within a reasonable time — normally 30 days.
      </p>
      <p>
        If you are not satisfied with our response, you can take the complaint to the
        Office of the Australian Information Commissioner at
        <a href="https://www.oaic.gov.au/" rel="noopener">oaic.gov.au</a> or on
        1300 363 992.
      </p>

      <h2>Other websites</h2>
      <p>
        Where this site links somewhere else — a government website, a Microsoft form,
        our Facebook or Instagram pages — that site has its own privacy policy and we have
        no control over it.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes</h2>
      <p>
        If this policy changes, the new version appears here with a new date at the top.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact us</h2>
      <p>
        <a href={`mailto:${EMAIL}`}>{EMAIL}</a><br />
        <a class="nowrap" href={PHONE_HREF}>{PHONE}</a><br />
        <span class="address">
          The Henley on Broadwater, {ADDRESS.street}, {ADDRESS.suburb} {ADDRESS.state}
          {' '}{ADDRESS.postcode}
        </span>
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .updated {
    font: var(--type-body-sm);
    color: var(--color-on-surface-secondary);
    margin-block-end: var(--space-xl);
  }

  .address {
    color: var(--color-on-surface-secondary);
  }

  .prose ol {
    padding-inline-start: var(--space-lg);
  }

  .prose ol li {
    margin-block-end: var(--space-md);
  }
</style>
